    "body": "<details><summary>AI feedback</summary>\r\n\r\n### Open / proposed items\r\n\r\n* D1: `<form>` has `HTML element removing steps` but no `HTML element moving steps`. On `<table><form id=\"f\"><tr><td><input id=\"i\"></table></form>`, calling `shadowRoot.moveBefore(f, null)` moves `f` into a different tree without running `removing steps`, leaving `i.form` in light DOM pointing to `f` inside `shadowRoot` (whereas `shadowRoot.appendChild(f)` and `shadowRoot.moveBefore(i, null)` both reset it, and Chrome already resets `i.form` to `null`).\r\nSuggested fix: Add `HTML element moving steps` for `form` matching its `HTML element removing steps`, and add a WPT case for `moveBefore()` across shadow trees.\r\n\r\n* D2: `form`'s `HTML element removing steps` iterate `For each form-associated element` without a specified order, and run in step 3 of the HTML `removing steps` before `reset the form owners with a form attribute` in step 5. On `<form id=\"f\"></form><order-face id=\"first\" form=\"f\"></order-face><order-face id=\"second\" form=\"f\"></order-face>`, removing `f` now resets `first` and `second` in step 3 in an unspecified order (making step 5 a no-op), so `formAssociatedCallback` order is no longer guaranteed to be tree order (Chrome currently fires `second` before `first`).\r\nSuggested fix: Iterate `inclusive descendant`s of `oldAncestor`'s `root` whose `form owner` is `removedNode`, `in tree order`, and add a WPT case for `formAssociatedCallback` order.\r\n\r\n* D3: Missing WPT coverage in `web-platform-tests/wpt#65040` for `<input type=\"image\">` (a non-`listed` `form-associated element` excluded from `form.elements`) and same-tree `moveBefore()` (which per spec should keep `input.form === form`, though Chrome currently resets it to `null`).\r\nSuggested fix: Add subtests for `<input type=\"image\">` and same-tree `moveBefore()` to `form-removal-resets-form-owner.html`.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Reviewed commits</summary>\r\n\r\nReviewed at 4b33003 on 823898c, with web-platform-tests/wpt#65040 at df893d6, using spec-pr-review.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n</details>",
